    "Dog park": {
      "comment": "Category for fenced dog parks"
    },
    "Dog parks and \"go meet everyone\" creates excitement, not calm. At 8 months she's lunging at every dog she sees — which started as over-socialization.": {
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Hondenparken en \"ga iedereen ontmoeten\" creëert opwinding, geen kalmte. Op 8 maanden hapt ze naar elke hond die ze ziet — wat begon als oversocialisatie."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Dog self-discovers": {
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Hond ontdekt zelf"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Dog-friendly park": {
      "comment": "Category for general dog-friendly parks",
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Hondvriendelijk park"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Dogs are forgiving. They don't need perfection — they need consistency. If you're roughly right, roughly often, they'll figure out the pattern.": {
      "comment": "Explanation of the forgiving nature of dogs, emphasizing the importance of consistency over perfection in training.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Honden zijn vergevingsgezind. Ze hebben geen perfectie nodig — ze hebben consistentie nodig. Als je ongeveer goed, ongeveer vaak bent, ontdekken ze het patroon."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Dogs don't generalize well. To them, \"down in the living room\" and \"down at the beach\" are genuinely different skills. The smells are different. The surface is different. The distractions are different.": {
      "comment": "Explanation of why dogs struggle to generalize skills learned in one environment to another.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Honden generaliseren niet goed. Voor hen zijn \"af in de woonkamer\" en \"af op het strand\" echt verschillende vaardigheden. De geuren zijn anders. Het oppervlak is anders. De afleidingen zijn anders."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Dogs met": {},
    "Dogs who follow you everywhere (room to room, up and down stairs) learn the opposite of independence. The crate prevents this.": {
      "comment": "Tip in the Training.CrateTraining section about the benefits of keeping a dog in a crate.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Honden die je overal volgen (kamer naar kamer, trap op en af) leren het tegenovergestelde van onafhankelijkheid. De bench voorkomt dit."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Don't forget to log %@'s day": {
      "comment": "A reminder to log a pet's day. The argument is the pet's name.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Vergeet niet de dag van %@ te loggen"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Don't have a link yet? Ask them to share from Settings → Family Sharing.": {
      "comment": "Hint text in the \"Awaiting invite\" view, instructing the user to ask the dog owner to share the invite link from the Family Sharing settings.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Heb je nog geen link? Vraag hen om te delen via Instellingen → Familiedeling."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Don't let your puppy push your hand away. Maintain gentle contact. They'll try to lick and dig at your fingers — hold steady. Click for any downward movement: nose dipping, an elbow bending, weight shifting.": {
      "comment": "Training tip for the 'Down' skill: advice on maintaining contact with the handler during training.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Laat je puppy je hand niet wegduwen. Houd zacht contact. Ze zullen proberen te likken en aan je vingers te graven — hou vol. Klik voor elke neerwaartse beweging: neus dippend, een elleboog buigend, gewicht verschuivend."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Don't punish accidents": {
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Straf ongelukjes niet"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Don't push your hand into their face": {
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Duw je hand niet in hun gezicht"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Don't push your hand into their face - let them come to you": {
      "comment": "Tip for the 'Touch & Handling' skill.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Duw je hand niet in hun gezicht - laat ze naar jou komen"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Don't take it personally.": {
      "comment": "Advice on how to handle the frustration of an adolescent dog.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Neem het niet persoonlijk."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Don't train during the whole walk. Dedicate training to short, focused sessions. Walks are for experiencing the world.": {
      "comment": "Tip for the \"Loose Leash Walking\" skill: advice on how to train during a walk.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Train niet tijdens de hele wandeling. Wijdt training aan korte, gefocuste sessies. Wandelingen zijn om de wereld te ervaren."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Don't train during walks. Walks are for sniffing, exploring, experiencing the world. Training happens in short, focused sessions — ideally at your doorstep or in your living room.": {
      "comment": "Explanation of why training should not happen during walks.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Train niet tijdens wandelingen. Wandelingen zijn om te snuffelen, verkennen, de wereld te ervaren. Training gebeurt in korte, gefocuste sessies — ideaal bij je voordeur of in je woonkamer."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Don't worry about perfecting this — name recognition naturally fades as the name becomes 'just a word' they hear all day": {
      "comment": "Tip for the Training.Skills.NameRecognition section, emphasizing that name recognition naturally improves over time.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Maak je geen zorgen over perfectie — naamherkenning vervaagt natuurlijk naarmate de naam 'gewoon een woord' wordt dat ze de hele dag horen"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Don't worry about sit vs stand vs down — position doesn't matter, only the eye contact.": {
      "comment": "Tip for the \"Watch Me\" skill, emphasizing that the focus should be on eye contact rather than the specific training positions.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Maak je geen zorgen over zit vs sta vs af — positie maakt niet uit, alleen het oogcontact."
          }
        }
      }
    },
