    "Ideal": {
      "comment": "Description of a body condition score when the user is at an ideal weight.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Ideaal"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If a behavior is no longer rewarded, it disappears. If variably rewarded (sometimes yes, sometimes no), it persists forever — the 'slot machine effect' keeps dogs eager. Phase out constant rewards, but never stop rewarding entirely.": {
      "comment": "Tip on using a variable reward system with dogs.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Als een gedrag niet meer wordt beloond, verdwijnt het. Als het variabel wordt beloond (soms wel, soms niet), blijft het voor altijd bestaan — het 'gokautomaateffect' houdt honden gretig. Bouw constante beloningen af, maar stop nooit helemaal met belonen."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If a behavior is rewarded every time, and then the rewards stop, the behavior disappears quickly.": {
      "comment": "Explanation of a behavioral psychology principle: if a behavior is rewarded every time, and then the rewards stop, the behavior disappears quickly.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Als een gedrag elke keer wordt beloond, en de beloningen dan stoppen, verdwijnt het gedrag snel."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If luring doesn't work, switch to operant/shaping: click for any movement toward the ground — nose dipping, one elbow bending, looking down. No pushing.": {
      "comment": "Alternative method to teach the 'down' skill, using positive reinforcement (clicks) for desired movements.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Als lokken niet werkt, schakel over naar operant/vormen: klik voor elke beweging naar de grond — neus dippend, een elleboog buigend, naar beneden kijkend. Niet duwen."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If puppy freezes, lure them forward with treats": {
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Als puppy bevriest, lok ze vooruit met snoepjes"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If recall fails, don't repeat the word. Walk closer, show the treat, and try again later with less distraction. Protect the magic word's power": {
      "comment": "Tip for practicing the \"come\" skill: what to do if the dog doesn't come when called.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Als terugroep faalt, herhaal het woord niet. Loop dichterbij, toon het snoepje, en probeer later opnieuw met minder afleiding. Bescherm de kracht van het toverwoord"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If they break, simply reset without punishment. The consequence is: you don't come back and reward yet.": {
      "comment": "Tip for the \"Stay\" skill: how to handle a break in the training session.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Als ze breken, reset gewoon zonder straf. De consequentie is: je komt nog niet terug om te belonen."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If they lose interest, use higher value treats": {
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Als ze interesse verliezen, gebruik hoogwaardigere snoepjes"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If training isn't working, try switching to kibble as treats. Fresh food can make them picky.": {
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Als training niet werkt, probeer over te schakelen naar brokjes als snoepjes. Vers voedsel kan ze kieskeurig maken."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If you click by accident, still give a treat to maintain the association": {
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Als je per ongeluk klikt, geef toch een snoepje om de associatie te behouden"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If you click by accident, still give a treat — maintaining the association is more important than perfect timing.": {
      "comment": "A tip related to the clicker training, emphasizing the importance of maintaining the association even if the click is accidental.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Als je per ongeluk klikt, geef toch een snoepje — de associatie behouden is belangrijker dan perfecte timing."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If your dog has passed away...": {
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Als je hond is overleden..."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If your dog is struggling, it's not their fault. It's too hard.": {
      "comment": "Text explaining the Step-Back Rule.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Als je hond moeite heeft, is het niet hun schuld. Het is te moeilijk."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If your dog jumps, your hand is too high. If they lose interest, lower the hand and make it easier.": {
      "comment": "Tip for the \"Loose Leash Walking\" skill.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Als je hond springt, is je hand te hoog. Als ze interesse verliezen, verlaag de hand en maak het makkelijker."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If your dog screams in the crate, that means you're using it too little, not that it doesn't work. Put them in more often — it gets calmer with use.": {
      "comment": "Encouragement to use the crate more often if your dog screams in it, as this indicates they're not using it enough.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Als je hond schreeuwt in de bench, betekent dat dat je hem te weinig gebruikt, niet dat het niet werkt. Zet ze er vaker in — het wordt kalmer met gebruik."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If your dog struggles, go back to an easier step. Success builds confidence.": {
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Als je hond moeite heeft, ga terug naar een makkelijkere stap. Succes bouwt vertrouwen op."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If your pup pulls toward distractions, become more interesting! Use treats and engagement.": {
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Als je pup naar afleidingen trekt, word interessanter! Gebruik snoepjes en betrokkenheid."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If your puppy backs up instead of sitting, practice with their back against a wall or in a corner - the only option becomes sitting down": {
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Als je puppy achteruit gaat in plaats van te zitten, oefen met hun rug tegen een muur of in een hoek - de enige optie wordt gaan zitten"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If your puppy keeps going behind you, sit with your back against a wall or couch.": {
      "comment": "Training tip for the \"Watch Me\" skill: if the puppy continues to go behind the trainer, sit with the trainer against a wall or couch.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true,
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Als je puppy steeds achter je gaat, zit met je rug tegen een muur of bank."
          }
        }
      }
    },
