    "Once a skill is solid (8 out of 10 times in multiple environments), start varying the rewards:": {
      "comment": "Explanation of what to do once a skill is solid in the \"Taking It Further\" module of the Foundations extension.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true
    },
    "Once reliable, add a sit after they arrive. One treat for coming, one treat for sitting. This prevents the 'drive-by' where your dog runs past you.": {
      "comment": "Training skill content: how to progress from a reliable \"come\" to adding a \"sit\" after the dog arrives.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true
    },
    "Once the behavior is reliable, you can add the verbal cue 'wait' to formalize it.": {
      "comment": "Tip for adding a verbal cue (\"wait\") to a reliable behavior like waiting at doors.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true
    },
    "Once the hand is behind your back, click and reward for eye contact. You should be able to walk at least 10 straight meters with your dog looking at your face before moving to forward starts.": {
      "comment": "How-to step for Training.LooseLeashWalking.howTo8.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true
    },
