    "This is me": {},
    "This is normal. This is biology.": {
      "comment": "Explanation of why dogs forget skills in the Training.Foundations.TakingFurther.forgetPara1 section.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true
    },
    "This is not failure. This is adolescence.": {
      "comment": "Explanation of the \"Adolescent Regression\" concept, emphasizing that it is a normal part of a dog's development.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true
    },
    "This is optional — you can always add one later.": {},
    "This is practical safety training — you don't want a dog bolting out the front door into traffic.": {
      "comment": "How-to step in the \"Wait\" training section, emphasizing the importance of safety.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true
    },
    "This is their story. Not all of it — the best parts happened between the logged moments. The head on your lap. The excited spin at the door. The way they looked at you.\n\nThose don't need an app to remember.": {},
    "This is totally normal! Dogs often need refreshers, especially during adolescence. A few quick sessions will get things back on track.": {},
    "This is your daily dashboard. See today's events, log meals, potty, sleep, and more.": {},
    "This isn't about obedience. It's about communication. Partnership. A relationship built on mutual understanding.": {
      "comment": "Paragraph 2 in the \"Let's Begin\" section of the Foundations module.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true
    },
    "This isn't failure. This is how learning works.": {
      "comment": "Reassurance text for the \"Why Dogs \\\"Forget\\\"\" section of the \"Taking It Further\" module.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true
    },
    "This member will be removed. Events they logged will keep their attribution.": {},
    "This might be the most important thing you learn:": {
