    "You do nothing except observe and click for desired behavior. Hands behind your back. No luring, no pushing, no verbal cues. You simply wait. The dog figures things out on its own, and you mark the moment it happens. This creates deep, lasting learning.": {
      "comment": "Explanation of the Operant Conditioning method.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true
    },
    "You do nothing. Hands behind your back. You wait. When the dog happens to do what you want, you mark and reward. The dog figures it out themselves.": {
      "comment": "Description of the operant training method.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated": true
    },
    "You guide the dog with a treat lure. The luring motion becomes the hand signal.": {
