    "Your Trial Has Ended": {},
    "Your daily command center": {},
    "Your dog doesn't understand English. When you say \"look at me\" while they're sniffing the floor, they associate those words with... sniffing the floor. The command becomes meaningless noise.\n\nIt works the other way around: first you teach them to offer the behavior, then you add the verbal cue. You'll learn exactly how soon enough!": {
      "comment": "Explanation of the correct way to teach a dog to look at you using the \"Look at me\" quiz question.",
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Je hond begrijpt geen Nederlands. Als je \"kijk naar mij\" zegt terwijl ze aan de grond snuffelen, associëren ze die woorden met... aan de grond snuffelen. Het commando wordt betekenisloze ruis.\n\nHet werkt andersom: eerst leer je ze het gedrag aan te bieden, dan voeg je het verbale commando toe. Je leert precies hoe, binnenkort!"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Your dog doesn't understand that you're repeating yourself. They think \"sit-sit-SIT\" is one long command. And they're learning that the cue involves you sounding increasingly upset.\n\nThere's a better way — one that doesn't involve words at all (at first). You'll discover the secret soon!": {
      "comment": "Explanation of the \"Word Trap\" quiz question and its answer options.",
      "localizations": {
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Je hond begrijpt niet dat je jezelf herhaalt. Ze denken dat \"zit-zit-ZIT\" één lang commando is. En ze leren dat het commando inhoudt dat jij steeds gefrustreerder klinkt.\n\nEr is een betere manier — eentje die helemaal geen woorden gebruikt (in het begin). Je ontdekt het geheim binnenkort!"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Your dog drops everything and sprints to you when they hear the magic word, even with major distractions.": {
      "comment": "Description of when a dog is ready to be called using a magic word.",
